{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-158357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X>1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{27}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x>3,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1) & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{4}{27}(3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{\\int }_{1}^{3}3{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}{[{x}^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}([(3)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(3)^{4}]-[(1)^{3}-\\frac{1}{4}(1)^{4}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}(27-\\frac{81}{4}-1+\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{27}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158357" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4918712cc933697d39bbe4d720ab030180ffbbfd7206f82ff2ea12ccab6a89c8"} {"question" "q-158357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{16}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{22}{27}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{9}"] ["math" "\\frac{8}{9}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158357" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{9}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(X\\le 2)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{72}({x}^{3}+x),\\, & 0\\le x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSince $f(x)$ is identical to zero for all $x<0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{72}({x}^{3}+x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}([\\frac{1}{4}(2)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{4}(0)^{4}+\\frac{1}{2}(0)^{2}]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{72}(4+2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{72} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158363" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4918712cc933697d39bbe4d720ab030180ffbbfd7206f82ff2ea12ccab6a89c8"} {"question" "q-158363" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158363" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{24}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{12}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{24}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158363" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(0\\le X<1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3},\\, & 0\\le x<2, \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}x & 2\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{32}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}({1}^{4}-{0}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158416" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4918712cc933697d39bbe4d720ab030180ffbbfd7206f82ff2ea12ccab6a89c8"} {"question" "q-158416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{16}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{32}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{32}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{8}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{16}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158416" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{32}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(2\\le X\\le 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}({x}^{3}-x),\\, & 1\\le x<2, \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}(x-1) & 2\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2\\le X\\le 3) & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{3}\\frac{1}{6}(x-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}-x]}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}([\\frac{1}{2}(3)^{2}-(3)]-[\\frac{1}{2}(2)^{2}-2]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{9}{2}-3-2+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158418" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4918712cc933697d39bbe4d720ab030180ffbbfd7206f82ff2ea12ccab6a89c8"} {"question" "q-158418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{6}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{4}"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{6}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158418" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute $P(2<X<4)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{20}\\sqrt{x},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{20}({x}^{2}-1) & 1<x\\le 4, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(2<X<4) & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{20}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}-x]}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}([\\frac{1}{3}(4)^{3}-(4)]-[\\frac{1}{3}(2)^{3}-(2)]) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(\\frac{64}{3}-4-\\frac{8}{3}+2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(\\frac{50}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158431" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4918712cc933697d39bbe4d720ab030180ffbbfd7206f82ff2ea12ccab6a89c8"} {"question" "q-158431" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068712/state.json" "file_sha256" "737f020d91f3defc4cc3383739d3efc94c21f71e537443d113714df150e71d04"} {"question" "q-158431" "field" "